From 94479dfce5814f7bcc23e8691c400f5b4add5a5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crazynucfan <127292955+crazynucfan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:57:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: apollo_defconfig: Realtek RTL8152 USB Ethernet driver

Without CONFIG_USB_RTL8152 an RTL8153 adapter binds to r8153_ecm, the
chip's CDC ECM configuration. In that mode the chip's receive filter
keeps the adapter's own MAC: an address set from Linux (a systemd .link
MACAddress=, which the node setup uses for a stable DHCP identity) is
never programmed into the chip, so every unicast frame to it is dropped,
promiscuous mode or not. DHCP and ARP replies to broadcasts still work,
which makes the failure look like a routing problem.

r8152 switches the adapter to its vendor configuration and programs the
MAC into the chip, as on negroni and rhodep. r8153_ecm stays built for
adapters r8152 does not claim.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/apollo_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/apollo_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/apollo_defconfig
index f842b341f..db6cff3f4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/apollo_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/apollo_defconfig
@@ -579,6 +579,7 @@ CONFIG_MDIO_BUS_MUX_MULTIPLEXER=y
 CONFIG_MDIO_BUS_MUX_MMIOREG=y
 CONFIG_USB_PEGASUS=m
 CONFIG_USB_RTL8150=m
+CONFIG_USB_RTL8152=m
 CONFIG_USB_USBNET=m
 CONFIG_USB_NET_DM9601=m
 CONFIG_USB_NET_SR9800=m
-- 
2.53.0

